ckground:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#fbbf24;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:6px;\"\u003eForward Risk\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eThe FOMC meeting runs September 15-16, with the official calendar giving the September 16 press conference at 2:30 PM ET. Wednesday adds retail sales, inventories, WPSR, and the press conference; Thursday adds housing and gas storage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eOmissions and Watch\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOmitted:\u003c/strong\u003e BLS official schedule access returned HTTP 403/access denied, so CPI, PPI, employment, and other BLS events were not inferred. BEA shows no release for 2026-09-14. NAR was not required for the verified calendar, and NYSE showed no Sep 14 holiday or shortened session.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUnscheduled Treasury rows:\u003c/strong\u003e TreasuryDirect lists a Sep 16 17-week Bill and Sep 17 4-week and 8-week Bills, but their API records had blank closing times at verification, so they were omitted under the exact-time rule. The FOMC meeting row has no standalone statement time; only the Sep 16 2:30 PM press conference was selected.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWatch:\u003c/strong\u003e WPSR is at 10:30 AM ET Wednesday and Natural Gas Storage at 10:30 AM ET Thursday. MOVE is above 80, shifting the signal from calm to moderate uncertainty.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eTrading Strategy Note - ES Futures\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #34d399;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#34d399;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eBase Case\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eES is 7621.50 overnight against a 764.29 SPY close. The 9:30 AM Bowman speech and 11:00/11:30 AM bill closings are the first decision windows; H.10/H.15 at 4:15 PM is the final rates check. NFCI remains loose and SOFR is 3.62%, but MOVE at 82.21 is moderate uncertainty, 10Y at 4.96% is restrictive, and WTI near 102.97 argues for smaller size and no chasing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #f87171;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#f87171;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eInvalidation\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eLose 7590 and hold below it, or see 10Y above 5.05% and MOVE back above 90, and the constructive bias is invalidated. A weak bill auction, further oil acceleration, or a hawkish response around the FOMC press conference also invalidates continuation assumptions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e"}